ees fahrenheit pretty easily so  that's what i would shoot for  some other special specialized features  depending on what you're trying to wash  from a glassware standpoint um whether  you have wide mouth or narrow neck  glassware direct injection spindles uh  are going to be very important what this  allows for is to  um to properly clean erlenmeyer flask  and other narrow neck glassware by  injecting a wash rinse uh water into  that piece of glassware to thoroughly  clean the inside of that so you're not  so you're  removing residual  reagent or sample  also this allows when it comes to drying  to  go ahead and provide forced air drying  into that glassware to make sure the  inside is properly dried as well  when it comes to that drying phase or  that drying step of  of that wash program  really need to  be in the 70 to 80 degrees c range to  quickly dry glassware  very important you don't want to wait  all day just  to have dry glassware  also worth mentioning  the ability to incorporate pure water  rinses  again there are some washing procedures  that um  recommend it there are other ones that  require it having a glassware washer  that can accommodate uh  a pure water rinse from pure from a  water purification  unit is important because that further  removes impurities that might remain on  glassware  additionally  on the user interface  of the glassware washer is very very  important  being able to interact with something um  making sure it's user friendly easy to  navigate is important because  we  because  user frustration  should always be be limited right  in the case of having standardized  procedures or wash procedures it's  important to have the ability to data  log and export that data just to have a  running tally or a track record and  making sure that you're hitting the  measures that you need to hit  and then additionally clear and specific  alarms um not having  um to go reference a manual somewhere  else to see what's going on with your  glasswa